# Honest omissions - concepts left unmapped, with the reason on record:
#   lo:ComicPoetRole: Wikidata has no item for the ancient comic poet as an occupation; mapping to poet or playwright would lose exactly the distinction the role encodes
#   lo:TragicPoetRole: Wikidata has no item for the ancient tragic poet as an occupation; same policy as the comic poet
#   lo:SuccessionsWriterRole: the diadochai author is a genre-specific role of Hellenistic historiography of philosophy with no Wikidata occupation item
#   lo:ExtantStatus: Wikidata models lost and fragmentary works as classes but has no concept for the unmarked extant case
#   lo:TechnicalTopic: a heterogeneous handbook bucket (tactics, agriculture, cookery, mechanics); any single Wikidata topic would misdescribe most of its works
#   lo:Asserted: the certainty levels encode Diogenes Laertius' own epistemic stances; Wikidata's epistemology items describe modern concepts, not this editorial axis
#   lo:Reported: same policy as lo:Asserted
#   lo:Disputed: same policy as lo:Asserted
#   lo:Conjectured: same policy as lo:Asserted
#   lo:Authentic: the authenticity verdicts are curator judgments on individual letters; Wikidata has no matching concept triple (literary forgery describes works, not verdicts)
#   lo:DisputedAuthenticity: same policy as lo:Authentic
#   lo:Spurious: same policy as lo:Authentic
